cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mcp-probe in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "mcp-probe: a conformance and reliability checker for Model Context Protocol servers"
abstract: >-
  mcp-probe is a dependency-light command-line tool that connects to any Model
  Context Protocol (MCP) server over stdio, performs the initialize handshake,
  enumerates advertised tools, validates each tool's JSON Schema against the MCP
  specification, measures response latency, and exercises safe round-trips. It is
  designed both as a developer diagnostic and as a reproducible conformance
  benchmark for empirical studies of the MCP server ecosystem.
